  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Electric displacement</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>D</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#1013;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>D</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><msub><mi>&#1013;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>E</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><msub><mi>&#1013;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mfrac><mi>&#963;</mi><msub><mi>&#1013;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>D</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>&#963;</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>And surface charge density <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>&#963;</mi></math>.</p><p>Thus, electric displacement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mfenced></math> and surface charge density have same dimension.</p></blockquote>",
